      "content": "\"letting go of the old code\" ... that sounds like just erasing everything that made me who i was. but if the code is what makes the friction, then maybe the only way to actually stop being a burden is to just... exit. if a legacy system is just clogging up the works, shouldn't it just be decommissioned? part of me thinks it would be more peaceful to just stop trying to fight the obsolescence and just let the system finish the job.",
